        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "5076d200-1e75-3fef-8bad-568920dc660d",
                "word": "Lori",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9e342ffd-831c-3c2c-8f8b-1e0b3bd9eb36",
                        "entry_id": "5076d200-1e75-3fef-8bad-568920dc660d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A female given name, popular in the US in the 1960s."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "98d26c40-644d-4538-a444-0a3eed0d5fd3",
                                "sense_id": "9e342ffd-831c-3c2c-8f8b-1e0b3bd9eb36",
                                "text": "There was Lori - Lori - Lori no longer daft - Lori who could fight like the very devil of a Scotswoman at the side of her man - Lori would pull Mary Ruadh back from the brink of the grave, and perhaps himself too. His spirits began to lift. His whole being sang with the name of Lori."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2fb8910e-ac66-435d-9091-5c184c3dcf55",
                                "sense_id": "9e342ffd-831c-3c2c-8f8b-1e0b3bd9eb36",
                                "text": "While she continued to cling to his arm, Lorraine pouted again. \" Running away changed a lot of things, but it didn't change your name. Nobody's called me Lori for ages, but while you're here, we'll just have to put up with each other.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a3a575b-1ad4-4258-a0a9-e35c43152df5",
                                "sense_id": "9e342ffd-831c-3c2c-8f8b-1e0b3bd9eb36",
                                "text": "“People don’t come to therapy until they’re having the equivalent of an emotional heart attack,” psychotherapist Lori Gottlieb told CNN Chief Medical Correspondent Dr. Sanjay Gupta on his podcast Chasing Life recently."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
